The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_UNCLOCKED);
cpu_do_idle();
```
Reason:
The CPU sets the state to 'WAIT_UNCLOCKED' and enters idle mode, which stops the local timer. If another CPU enters 'WFI' during this time, the local timer interrupt does not fire, preventing the CPU in 'WAIT_UNCLOCKED' from waking up at the expected time.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (++num_idle_cpus == num_online_cpus())
    imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_UNCLOCKED);
if (num_idle_cpus-- == num_online_cpus())
    imx6_set_lpm(WAIT_CLOCKED);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the CPU transitions to 'WAIT_CLOCKED' when all CPUs are idle, allowing the local timer to remain active and ensuring that the CPU can wake up at the expected time using the local timer interrupt instead of an unrelated interrupt.

